    "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nFix `NotImplementedError: W4A8 Int8 MoE is only supported on CPU platforms` when\r\nserving a compressed-tensors checkpoint whose MoE experts are quantized\r\nINT4-weight / INT8-dynamic-activation on CUDA.\r\n\r\nCUDA has no native W4A8-INT MoE kernel: such layers currently reach\r\n`CompressedTensorsW4A8Int8MoEMethod`, whose backend oracle\r\n`select_w4a8_int8_moe_backend` is CPU-only and raises on CUDA.\r\n\r\nThis PR routes those layers to `CompressedTensorsWNA16MoEMethod` on CUDA: the\r\nINT4 weights run on the existing WNA16 Marlin MoE kernel, which quantizes\r\nactivations to INT8 per token at runtime. No new kernel is added — it is a\r\ndispatch change inside the existing `_is_dynamic_token_w4a8_int` branch, so the\r\nCPU path is untouched.\r\n\r\nINT8 activation quantization is opt-in and requires\r\n`VLLM_MARLIN_INPUT_DTYPE=int8`. When that variable is unset the same weights run\r\nas W4A16, i.e. existing WNA16 behavior is unchanged.\r\n\r\nThis is not a duplicate: no open PR routes compressed-tensors W4A8-INT MoE to\r\nWNA16 on CUDA; existing W4A8 work covers FP8 (`CompressedTensorsW4A8Fp8MoEMethod`)\r\nand the CPU path only.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n- `VLLM_MARLIN_INPUT_DTYPE` unset → CUDA loads the layer as WNA16/W4A16; no\r\n  `NotImplementedError`.\r\n- `VLLM_MARLIN_INPUT_DTYPE=int8` → same layer loads as WNA16 with INT8\r\n  activations (info log line above appears once).\r\n- CPU (or `current_platform` non-CUDA) selects\r\n  `CompressedTensorsW4A8Int8MoEMethod`.\r\n\r\n",
